  "conclusion": "At the finite-beta stress radius the correction has the right sign but applies less momentum correction than the Redl target would require. Increasing Pmax reduces the stress error monotonically, but the P=12 reduced closure remains above the 1e-1 current gate. The stress-radius current is also a cancellation-dominated species-current observable, so small species-flow imbalances are amplified in the net current.",
